      "message": "Nit — a few minor tag/attribute edge cases here:\n1. `SUMMARY_TAG` starts with `^[ \\t]*`, so a blank line between `\u003cdetails\u003e` and `\u003csummary\u003e` (common in GitHub-flavored markdown) prevents `\u003csummary\u003e` from matching and renders it as escaped text. Using `^\\s*` handles that.\n2. Both `OPEN_TAG` and `SUMMARY_TAG` use `\\b`, which also matches hyphenated custom elements like `\u003cdetails-foo\u003e` / `\u003csummary-bar\u003e`; `(?\u003d[\\s\u003e])` avoids that.\n3. `OPEN_ATTR` scans the raw attribute string without skipping quoted values, so `\u003cdetails title\u003d\"leave open\"\u003e` would falsely set `open`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "34affc02636a50c981c24e97fb16c08cd9bf4561",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
