      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T10:16:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`findClosingTag` counts `\u003cdetails\u003e` / `\u003c/details\u003e` occurrences inside fenced code blocks (``` / ~~~) and inline code spans (backticks). In code review comments (e.g. HTML/markdown diffs or docs mentioning `\u003cdetails\u003e`), this either closes the block prematurely mid-fence or leaves `depth \u003e 0` and falls back to escaped plaintext for the whole section.\n\nAlso, `\u003cdetails\\b` matches hyphenated custom elements like `\u003cdetails-foo\u003e` because `-` is a word boundary — `\u003cdetails(?\u003d[\\s\u003e])` is safer.\n\nCould we skip fenced code blocks and inline backtick spans while scanning in `findClosingTag` and add unit tests for both?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "34affc02636a50c981c24e97fb16c08cd9bf4561",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
