      "side": 1,
      "message": "`marked` calls `start(src.slice(1))` to find where a block extension interrupts a paragraph. Because `/^ {0,3}\u003cdetails\\b/i` has no multiline/newline anchor:\n\n1. It never matches a `\u003cdetails\u003e` on a subsequent line after a paragraph without a blank line.\n2. For inline text like `a\u003cdetails\u003efoo\u003c/details\u003e`, `src.slice(1)` starts at `\u003cdetails\u003e`, so `start()` returns `0`, splitting `a` into its own `\u003cp\u003ea\u003c/p\u003e` and turning the inline `\u003cdetails\u003e` into a block.\n\nMatching after a newline and using `(?\u003d[\\s\u003e])` instead of `\\b` (so custom elements like `\u003cdetails-foo\u003e` don\u0027t match) avoids both issues:\n```ts\nstart(src) {\n  const match \u003d /\\n {0,3}\u003cdetails(?\u003d[\\s\u003e])/i.exec(src);\n  return match ? match.index + 1 : undefined;\n},\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "34affc02636a50c981c24e97fb16c08cd9bf4561",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
